Defconfig done (task 9). Now the app (task 10). Let me rewrite ai_glasses_main.c to:
1. Generate a small WAV file (e.g., 1s, 8kHz, 16-bit mono sine wave) to /data/hello.wav
2. Call system("nxplayer /data/hello.wav")
3. Log the result

Let me write the app. I need to be careful with the WAV generation code — a valid WAV header + PCM data.

WAV header (44 bytes for PCM):
- "RIFF" + (36 + dataSize) + "WAVE"
- "fmt " + 16 + audioFormat(1=PCM) + numChannels(1) + sampleRate(8000) + byteRate + blockAlign + bitsPerSample(16)
- "data" + dataSize

Then the PCM data: 1 second at 8kHz = 8000 samples, 16-bit = 16000 bytes.

I'll write a helper `generate_wav(const char *path)` that creates this file.

The app:
```c
#include <nuttx/config.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <stdint.h>

#define WAV_SAMPLE_RATE 8000
#define WAV_DURATION_SEC 1

static int generate_wav(const char *path)
{
  FILE *fp;
  int i;
  int nsamples = WAV_SAMPLE_RATE * WAV_DURATION_SEC;
  uint32_t datasize = nsamples * 2; /* 16-bit mono */
  uint8_t header[44];

  memcpy(header, "RIFF", 4);
  header[4] = (36 + datasize) & 0xff;
  header[5] = ((36 + datasize) >> 8) & 0xff;
  header[6] = ((36 + datasize) >> 16) & 0xff;
